A corporate office uses four floors in a building, design and implement with 10.100.10.0 IP.
*Floor 1 has 50 users (VLAN101)
*Floor 2 has 30 users (VLAN102)
*Floor 3 has 14 users (VLAN103)
*Floor 4 has 6 users (VLAN104)

!@Floor 1 (VLAN101)
C: 50 = 6 bits
S: /32 - /6 = /26 (4th, 64i)
I: Ipasok sa 4th si 64

N: 10.100.10.64
F: 10.100.10.65
L: 10.100.10.126
B: 10.100.10.127

!@Floor 2 (VLAN102)
C: 30 = 5 bits
S: /32 - /5 = /27 (4th, 32i)
I: Ipasok sa 4th si 32

N: 10.100.10.128
F: 10.100.10.129
L: 10.100.10.158
B: 10.100.10.159

!@Floor 3 (VLAN103)
C: 14 = 4 bits
S: /32 - /4 = /28 (4th, 16i)
I: Ipasok sa 4th si 16

N: 10.100.10.160
F: 10.100.10.161
L: 10.100.10.174
B: 10.100.10.175

!@Floor 4 (VLAN104)
C: 6 = 3 bits
S: /32 - /3 = /29 (4th, 8i)
I: Ipasok sa 4th si 8

N: 10.100.10.176
F: 10.100.10.177
L: 10.100.10.182
B: 10.100.10.183

notFLOOR : 10.100.10.184

!@IMPLEMENTATION:

(FLOOR 1)(VLAN101)
!@A1
conf t
vlan 101
name VLAN101.COM
exit
int vlan 101
ip add 10.100.10.65 255.255.255.192
no shut

ip dhcp excluded-address 10.100.10.65 10.100.10.70
ip dhcp pool VLAN101.COM
network 10.100.10.64 255.255.255.192
default-router 10.100.10.65

int e0/0
switchport mode access
switchport access vlan 101
end

!@P1
conf t
int e0/0
no shut
ip add dhcp
end

